    },
    {
      "variantId": "B2",
      "strengths": "The thirteen-point selection combines useful subsystem coverage with explicit architectural perspectives. The editor preserves its modular, ownership, call, and dependency branches from tree to canvas. Persistence distinguishes workspace-manifest publication from catalog publication, while generation separates preparation, installation, and acknowledgement. Static analysis includes the useful diagram-leaf-to-concept-group boundary.",
      "weaknesses": "The same components recur across perspectives, and the persistence central tree still spans 98 lines with detailed thresholds, retry timings, and storage mechanics. Connections remain central-to-peripheral expansions rather than a visible network of collaborating responsibilities.",
      "improvementPotential": "High: retain the architectural distinctions while giving shared entities one concise description, moving parameter-level details outward, and adding meaningful connections between existing panels. Persistence and editor canvases offer concrete opportunities to improve readability without changing the selected points."
    },
    {
      "variantId": "C1",
      "strengths": "The fifteen points make useful separations between revisions and parsing, workspace ownership and native rendering, and validated generation and chat. The rendering overview contracts from 88 to 56 lines while retaining projection, settlement, history, and cleanup. Workspace edges explicitly connect session commits to record projection and then delivery, giving the canvas operational connectivity beyond expansion spokes.",
      "weaknesses": "Composition, canvas commands, and evaluation still have central trees of 99, 92, and 96 lines. Fine details such as camera defaults and shape dimensions compete with architectural explanations in peripherals. Splitting responsibilities across more points also creates repeated boundary descriptions.",
      "improvementPotential": "High: compress the three dense overviews, remove repeated boundary explanations, and extend the workspace canvas's meaningful connectivity to rendering and generation. The point selection and readable workflow hierarchy provide a strong foundation for focused refinement."
    },
    {
      "variantId": "C2",
      "strengths": "It retains C1's useful responsibility boundaries and adds explicit ownership and dependency perspectives. Workspace connections show optimistic-cache updates and editor remounts; the chat canvas connects captured history to isolated child controllers. The static-analysis canvas distinguishes analyzer execution from the static calls represented in its results.",
      "weaknesses": "Several overviews become substantially denser than C1: agent access reaches 108 lines, source evidence 103, and chat 104. Repeated perspective headings and detailed lifecycle descriptions make central and peripheral content harder to distinguish. The extra text does not consistently produce more meaningful connectivity.",
      "improvementPotential": "Compress repeated owners, inputs, and lifecycle steps while preserving the useful cross-panel links. Improvements are feasible, but selecting it alongside C1 would fund the same point selection twice, with much of the work devoted to reducing density."
    }
